**The main finding is that yesterday's measurement was partly wrong.** When I re-ran the site's own analysis with a correct exclusion rule, some results changed.
- **Many session records hold errors instead of answers.** 108 of the 1,220 scripted records have at least one answer replaced by the runner's "Daemon unreachable: HTTP Error 502/503" message. The 09-21 script only dropped records under 100 words, so it kept these partly failed records.
- **Legion's p=0.003 decline was one of them.** It becomes p=0.20 once those records are removed.
- **McNugget's Gemma 4 12B stretch can't be tested.** Only 4 of its 47 records have all six answers.
- **Corrected result:** 3 of 21 tests reach nominal p<0.05, their directions are mixed, and none survives correction. That is "no corrected trend", not "flat". The fourfold jump when the runner moved to the Rust daemon is unaffected.

